SUMMARY:Guelph Black Heritage Society - Reclaimed Routes Bus Tour; Exploring the Queen’s Bush
DESCRIPTION:Step aboard for a guided journey through the historic Queen’s Bush\, where Black freedom seekers established vibrant communities after escaping enslavement. \nAlong the route\, we’ll explore the stories of the families who built homes\, churches\, schools\, and cemeteries across what are now Waterloo Region and Wellington County. \nToday\, many of these sites have disappeared from the landscape\, but their history and legacy remain. \nThis tour offers an opportunity to uncover these often-overlooked stories and reflect on the resilience\, determination\, and contributions of early Black settlers in the region. \nDeparts: Heritage Hall\, 83 Essex Street\, Guelph \nTime: 12:00 PM (approximately 3 hours) \nCost: $25 per person (includes a picnic lunch) \nAdvance registration required. Tickets available on eventbrite.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/guelph-black-heritage-society-reclaimed-routes-bus-tour-exploring-the-queens-bush/
LOCATION:Heritage Hall\, Essex Street 83\, Guelph\, Ontario\, N1H 3K9\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Guelph Black Heritage Society":MAILTO:marketing.gbhs@gmail.com
GEO:43.5396806;-80.2503497
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Heritage Hall Essex Street 83 Guelph Ontario N1H 3K9 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=Essex Street 83:geo:-80.2503497,43.5396806
END:VEVENT
