SUMMARY:Kensington Market Historical Society - Kensington's Jewish Roots: A Guided Tour
DESCRIPTION:Specially presented for attendees of the Ashkenaz Festival\, this guided tour by the Kensington Market Historical Society (KMHS) bridges the gap between contemporary Yiddish culture and its deep-rooted heritage in Toronto. Taking place on Sunday\, August 30\, during the legendary Ashkenaz @ Pedestrian Sunday\, this tour explores how early Eastern European Jewish immigrants built the bustling open-air market that set the stage for generations of Jewish arts\, activism\, and community. Discover the physical and cultural foundations of the neighbourhood before enjoying the festival’s afternoon performances. \nStart: Baldwin and Augusta Stage
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/kensington-market-historical-society-kensingtons-jewish-roots-a-guided-tour/
LOCATION:Kensington Market\, 80 Bellevue Avenue\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5T 2N7\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Kensington Market Historical Society":MAILTO:info@kmhs.ca
GEO:43.6553269;-79.4039648
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Kensington Market 80 Bellevue Avenue Toronto Ontario M5T 2N7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=80 Bellevue Avenue:geo:-79.4039648,43.6553269
